THOUGHT: NullAway complains that textures and counts may be uninitialized. They are package-private and likely treated as @NonNull. The simplest safe fix is to initialize them to empty arrays in the constructor so they are always non-null, without changing behavior (they’ll be replaced when actually used). I’ll edit the file accordingly.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '1066,1069c\    public Cache(int id, int offset) {
      this.id = id;
      this.offset = offset;
      this.textures = new Texture[0];
      this.counts = new int[0];
    }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g2d/SpriteCache.java
```

